Check constraints: `n` is length of string? The loop goes to `n`. `substring(i)` implies `i` is index. Java `substring(i)` starts at index `i`. `charAt(j)` for `j` from `i-1` down to 0. So it reverses prefix of length `i`.
PHP `substr($t, 0, $i)` gets first `i` chars. `strrev` reverses. `substr($t, $i)` gets rest. Correct.

